# Must exist (even before the real entries below were added) so
# `npm pack`/`publish` doesn't fall back to treating .gitignore as its own
# exclusion list - that would silently drop docs/opencode-docs-reference/
# and deploy/models-dev-snapshot.json, both gitignored-but-git-tracked on
# purpose (see CLAUDE.md) and both things the offline target machine
# actually needs.
#
# vendor/ (the split JDK) is excluded from the root package's *normal*
# publish (the one release.yml runs automatically at the tag's real
# version, no --tag) - it's still published, just not there. Each part
# goes out separately as its own small, non-latest version instead
# (scripts/publish-jdk-parts.sh) - including it here too would blow the
# normal publish straight back past registry.npmjs.org's real per-publish
# payload ceiling (see docs/lessons-learned.md; this is exactly how
# v1.0.16 failed the first time).
#
# mcp-servers/java-lsp's and mcp-servers/spring-lsp's own vendored
# jdtls/spring-boot-language-server tarballs (~51MB/~81MB) are excluded
# for a different, size-independent reason: installing either MCP server
# always goes through its own separately-published
# @kealthas-dev/opencode-mcp-java-lsp/-spring-lsp package (which
# whitelists vendor/*.tar.gz in its own package.json "files" field), never
# through the root package, so carrying a second copy of either tarball
# here is pure waste regardless of the JDK question.
vendor/
mcp-servers/java-lsp/vendor/
mcp-servers/spring-lsp/vendor/
